WEBVTT

00:03.220 --> 00:04.760
You think these cookies will sell?

00:04.760 --> 00:07.310
Souma-kun designed that label.

00:07.310 --> 00:08.710
Isn't it cute?

00:08.710 --> 00:10.310
Yo, that's Sakura.

00:10.570 --> 00:11.270
Woof!

00:11.470 --> 00:13.490
She is a cute dog.

00:14.700 --> 00:16.570
We've got another kind, too.

00:15.740 --> 00:16.570
<b>Asami's friend 
who's helping
 out at the cafe</b>

00:17.090 --> 00:18.060
That's my drawing!

00:18.060 --> 00:19.030
It's cute, huh.

00:19.400 --> 00:21.780
When I draw, it comes out too clean.

00:21.780 --> 00:25.360
And I thought your dopey 
drawing would be cuter.

00:25.360 --> 00:26.510
Are you making fun of me?

00:26.510 --> 00:28.380
I'm really not!

00:28.910 --> 00:30.230
It's nothing groundbreaking,

00:30.230 --> 00:33.330
but I thought I'd start by
 doing what I can do now.

00:34.250 --> 00:35.420
Impressive.

00:35.720 --> 00:38.610
When you have a goal, every 
day is fulfilling, huh?

00:38.610 --> 00:39.390
Yes!

00:39.390 --> 00:42.150
Shun, you need to get your 
summer homework done.

00:42.150 --> 00:44.790
But Hayate-san isn't here yet.

00:44.790 --> 00:46.880
Then get started by yourself.

00:46.880 --> 00:47.490
I can't.

00:47.600 --> 00:48.690
<b>Hayate-san</b>

00:49.260 --> 00:50.520
Oh, speaking of.

00:51.170 --> 00:52.170
Hello.

00:52.170 --> 00:53.160
Is everything all right?

00:53.160 --> 00:54.350
<i>Hi, Shun-kun.</i>

00:54.350 --> 00:55.480
<i>I'm sorry I'm late.</i>

00:55.480 --> 00:57.350
It's not a big deal.

00:57.350 --> 01:00.540
<i>I couldn't find my phone, and 
looking for it made me late.</i>

01:00.540 --> 01:03.050
Well, I'm glad you found it.

01:03.050 --> 01:06.380
<i>Actually, I gave up. I'm on my way over now.</i>

01:08.030 --> 01:10.310
<i>So, how are you calling me now?</i>

01:10.310 --> 01:11.970
Huh? With my phone.

01:11.970 --> 01:13.220
<i>Huh?</i>

01:15.060 --> 01:16.270
I'm almost there.

01:16.270 --> 01:17.350
Okay.

01:17.910 --> 01:19.140
What's going on?

01:19.140 --> 01:22.800
Hayate-san was calling me on his 
phone while looking for his phone.

01:22.680 --> 01:23.220
<b>Spit!</b>

02:54.730 --> 02:55.920
All right.

02:55.770 --> 03:00.280
<b>#21 
Friends</b>

02:55.920 --> 02:57.210
I'm calling it a day.

02:57.210 --> 02:58.590
Thank you so much.

02:58.590 --> 02:59.790
You're leaving already?

02:59.790 --> 03:00.840
You got something to do?

03:00.840 --> 03:01.600
Yeah.

03:01.610 --> 03:08.830
<b>Listening...</b>

03:02.000 --> 03:07.150
A friend of mine is making their own CD, 
and I'm going to be designing the cover.

03:07.150 --> 03:08.840
We're meeting up to discuss it.

03:09.400 --> 03:10.810
See you all later.

03:11.750 --> 03:13.880
He was so excited.

03:14.670 --> 03:17.170
He seems like he's got so 
many things he wants to do.

03:17.170 --> 03:18.350
That's amazing.

03:18.680 --> 03:21.260
Hayate-san, do you have 
any plans for the future?

03:21.260 --> 03:22.920
Not yet.

03:23.190 --> 03:25.320
You could become a teacher or something.

03:25.320 --> 03:26.630
You're good at teaching.

03:27.510 --> 03:29.220
I've thought about it,

03:29.220 --> 03:31.690
but I'm not good at dealing 
with many people at once.

03:31.690 --> 03:32.970
True.

03:32.970 --> 03:34.180
They probably wouldn't warm up to you.

03:34.400 --> 03:35.270
<b>Ugh</b>

03:34.480 --> 03:35.270
<b>Stab</b>

03:36.320 --> 03:37.830
It's my summer break.

03:37.830 --> 03:39.480
I want to do something amazing.

03:39.480 --> 03:42.630
That's what you said last 
month too, on your birthday.

03:42.630 --> 03:44.060
I'm 17 now.

03:44.060 --> 03:45.280
I want to do something amazing.

03:45.530 --> 03:47.370
<i>Sounds like he'd say that 
no matter the occasion.</i>

03:47.660 --> 03:49.440
That's a surprise.

03:49.440 --> 03:52.090
Shun-kun seems like he'd be embarrassed
 by his family celebrating his birthday.

03:52.350 --> 03:55.410
Our mother really does love celebrations.

03:55.410 --> 03:58.920
Oh, that reminds me of what she told me...

03:58.920 --> 03:59.890
Shun?

03:59.890 --> 04:02.130
We're bringing out the 
cake, so please come down.

04:02.130 --> 04:04.760
Happy 17th birthday!

04:04.760 --> 04:06.800
So you're already 17.

04:06.800 --> 04:07.880
Time does fly.

04:07.880 --> 04:10.400
Come on, stop it.

04:10.400 --> 04:11.810
Don't treat me like a child.

04:11.810 --> 04:14.240
But to your father and me,

04:11.810 --> 04:16.900
Shun-kun
 Happy birthday

04:14.240 --> 04:16.910
you and your sister will 
always be our children.

04:17.230 --> 04:20.600
We've got to do these celebrations 
while you're still living here.

04:18.190 --> 04:19.610
<b>Hiragana,
 like for a child...</b>

04:21.010 --> 04:22.940
Here you go. Put on the candles.

04:22.940 --> 04:23.820
Candles?

04:23.820 --> 04:26.340
Come on, we don't have to do that.

04:26.340 --> 04:28.420
<i>...he says, but still takes them.</i>

04:28.970 --> 04:30.490
I'll go get a lighter.

04:30.490 --> 04:32.360
This is the last time, okay?

04:32.680 --> 04:34.750
But you still want a cake, right?

04:34.750 --> 04:36.160
I'll have cake.

04:36.160 --> 04:37.830
But no more candles after this year.

04:38.140 --> 04:39.850
Don't be like that.

04:39.850 --> 04:43.560
The candles on your cake 
only get lit once a year...

04:42.300 --> 04:44.260
Shun-kun
 Happy birthday

04:44.410 --> 04:46.730
They're all upside down.

04:47.290 --> 04:50.560
It's a symbol saying that 
I don't need them lit.

04:50.810 --> 04:52.260
Oh, you made a little mistake.

04:52.260 --> 04:53.840
No, it was on purpose.

04:53.840 --> 04:54.590
If you say so.

04:54.590 --> 04:55.910
Let's just turn them around.

04:55.910 --> 04:57.180
I told you!

04:57.180 --> 04:59.470
So that happened.

04:59.470 --> 05:01.500
Not that story again.

05:01.500 --> 05:03.520
It sounds like your family is close.

05:03.800 --> 05:06.390
Hayate-kun, are you going home for Obon?

05:07.400 --> 05:10.490
I was thinking of waiting a little 
later and going home in early September.

05:10.940 --> 05:12.290
Where were you from, again?

05:12.290 --> 05:13.190
Mie.

05:13.190 --> 05:14.170
Mie?

05:14.500 --> 05:16.530
Is that the place where they 
have that shrimp-like shrine?

05:16.530 --> 05:18.880
What part of Ise Jingū 
reminds you of shrimp?

05:21.170 --> 05:21.710
<b>Slam</b>

05:21.170 --> 05:21.710
<b>Slam</b>

05:21.420 --> 05:22.500
I'm done!

05:22.500 --> 05:23.840
Yeahhh

05:23.140 --> 05:24.730
But just with math.

05:24.730 --> 05:27.460
Want to do some reading for the 
book review for a change of pace?

05:27.830 --> 05:29.170
I want to be done.

05:29.550 --> 05:30.010
<b>Slump</b>

05:29.610 --> 05:31.950
I finished an entire manga series yesterday.

05:31.950 --> 05:32.970
Can that count?

05:33.180 --> 05:33.890
<b>Ignore</b>

05:33.240 --> 05:35.640
Oh, what about Igarashi-sensei's book?

05:35.950 --> 05:37.330
We saw the movie not long ago,

05:37.330 --> 05:39.100
so you could probably 
imagine the scenes easily.

05:39.360 --> 05:39.810
<b>Oh</b>

05:39.930 --> 05:42.300
I could just write a review 
based on the movie!

05:42.300 --> 05:45.320
But the book and the movie diverged 
quite a bit, so you'd get found out.

05:45.760 --> 05:48.780
You could just write it for me, Hayate-san.

05:49.390 --> 05:51.750
But it's a good book. 
I'd like you to read it.

05:51.750 --> 05:54.240
I'm too busy with sports.

05:54.240 --> 05:56.550
If you focused, you could 
get it done in half a day.

05:56.550 --> 05:58.400
No way it's taking me any less than a year.

05:58.750 --> 05:59.410
Hey.

05:59.710 --> 06:01.840
Since you won't do it for me,

06:01.840 --> 06:03.990
maybe I could learn what
 I need from the source.

06:04.540 --> 06:05.710
The source?

06:05.710 --> 06:06.620
Motoharu-san.

06:07.630 --> 06:10.420
Y-You can't do that! He's busy!

06:11.270 --> 06:12.680
He said he'd come over.

06:12.680 --> 06:13.330
What?

06:13.330 --> 06:14.810
He's so flexible...

06:15.090 --> 06:17.630
Thanks for your help today, Shiki-kun.

06:17.630 --> 06:19.120
I look forward to it!

06:19.120 --> 06:19.900
Cool.

06:20.480 --> 06:23.040
That wrapped up quickly, so
 maybe I'll go back to the cafe.

06:27.540 --> 06:29.110
<i>So many people are wearing yukatas...</i>

06:29.110 --> 06:31.570
<b>That reminds me!</b>

06:29.450 --> 06:31.580
<i>Today and tomorrow is the summer festival!</i>

06:31.580 --> 06:35.120
<i>I should invite Shun and Hayate-kun to come 
check out the stands with me this evening.</i>

06:35.120 --> 06:37.710
Oh, Motoharu-kun!

06:38.360 --> 06:39.760
Hey, Souma!

06:39.760 --> 06:40.580
How's it going?

06:40.580 --> 06:45.340
<b>Fast friends</b>

06:40.850 --> 06:42.180
It's good to see you.

06:42.180 --> 06:43.370
What are you doing here?

06:43.370 --> 06:44.680
Are you meeting someone?

06:44.680 --> 06:45.630
Nope.

06:45.630 --> 06:48.340
I lost my way and didn't 
know what to do next.

06:46.680 --> 06:51.590
<b>Ha  Ha</b>

06:48.340 --> 06:49.560
Wow.

06:49.560 --> 06:51.590
I wouldn't have guessed 
you were at a loss.

06:51.960 --> 06:53.280
Why not check the map on your phone?

06:53.280 --> 06:54.950
It's about to die.

06:54.950 --> 06:56.920
I've got three percent left.

06:56.920 --> 06:59.890
<i>I guess Motoharu-kun might be a dummy, too.</i>

07:00.790 --> 07:01.690
I'm back.

07:02.840 --> 07:03.980
Thanks for inviting me.

07:04.520 --> 07:05.960
You're done with your thing?

07:05.960 --> 07:06.560
Yeah.

07:07.030 --> 07:08.820
I heard the cafe is closed today,

07:08.820 --> 07:10.900
so I brought some cheesecake.

07:09.450 --> 07:15.040
<b>Heart Pounding</b>

07:10.900 --> 07:12.770
Please enjoy it together.

07:12.770 --> 07:15.030
Oh, wow, thank you so much.

07:15.280 --> 07:16.240
<b>Bow
Bow</b>

07:15.360 --> 07:17.120
Igarashi-sensei,

07:17.120 --> 07:19.630
thank you so much for coming here, 
despite your busy schedule.

07:19.980 --> 07:21.380
No problem at all.

07:21.380 --> 07:22.930
Are you working?

07:22.930 --> 07:23.850
I was.

07:24.350 --> 07:27.800
Shun, you're writing a book 
report about my novel?

07:27.800 --> 07:28.720
Yeah.

07:28.720 --> 07:30.300
I'm really happy to hear that.

07:30.610 --> 07:32.770
So, can you tell me what it's about, and—

07:32.770 --> 07:33.560
Here you go.

07:33.560 --> 07:34.270
Huh?

07:34.490 --> 07:36.220
Read it yourself.

07:36.220 --> 07:38.970
I'm not nice enough to 
help with your homework.

07:41.230 --> 07:42.960
When your review's done, let me read it.

07:42.960 --> 07:45.440
Hayate-kun, how long are you 
going to bow your head?

07:45.670 --> 07:48.290
I told you that I can't read books.

07:48.290 --> 07:50.440
That's rude to say in front of an author.

07:50.440 --> 07:52.190
If it's not a habit, it's hard, huh?

07:52.570 --> 07:53.770
Let me see it for a moment.

07:53.770 --> 07:54.530
Huh?

07:54.920 --> 07:57.230
I'll put a charm on it that'll motivate you.

07:57.570 --> 07:59.190
Really? Thanks!

07:59.750 --> 08:02.790
<i>He just teased me and is actually—</i>

08:02.870 --> 08:03.790
To Shun

08:02.870 --> 08:03.790
Igarashi
Motoharu

08:02.870 --> 08:03.790
Good luck!

08:02.870 --> 08:03.790
The Lost Diary
 Igarashi Motoharu

08:03.020 --> 08:03.800
Here you go.

08:03.790 --> 08:04.880
The Lost Diary
 Igarashi Motoharu

08:03.800 --> 08:04.880
To Shun

08:03.800 --> 08:04.880
Igarashi
Motoharu

08:03.800 --> 08:04.880
Good luck!

08:03.800 --> 08:04.890
I signed it.

08:05.800 --> 08:07.280
<i>Oh, wow! I'm so jealous!</i>

08:07.280 --> 08:08.830
I mean, thanks, but...

08:10.280 --> 08:11.640
What's so funny?

08:11.640 --> 08:12.670
I'm sorry.

08:13.020 --> 08:18.030
It's just, they both came 
to help you with your homework,

08:18.030 --> 08:19.610
like they're your older 
brothers or something.

08:19.610 --> 08:21.630
That made me think your youngest 
brother vibe was cute.

08:21.630 --> 08:23.240
It's not cute!

08:23.240 --> 08:24.820
Do not call me cute!

08:24.820 --> 08:25.850
Oh, sorry.

08:26.590 --> 08:30.450
But you're right, I do feel like 
I'm very lucky to have you around.

08:31.620 --> 08:32.920
So affectionate!

08:32.920 --> 08:33.860
Shut up!

08:34.110 --> 08:35.070
<b>Snap!</b>

08:34.420 --> 08:36.320
I'll read this in one second, 
so just leave me alone!

08:36.700 --> 08:37.780
It's upside down.

08:38.180 --> 08:40.840
That's on purpose! I can read like this too.

08:40.840 --> 08:43.500
Got it. You can flip it 
back when it gets hard.

08:44.590 --> 08:45.860
He flipped it back.

08:47.020 --> 08:49.820
Oh, yeah, so there's a 
festival going on today.

08:49.820 --> 08:50.520
Did you guys know?

08:50.520 --> 08:52.150
We didn't.

08:52.150 --> 08:53.730
Why don't we eat dinner at the festival stands?

08:53.730 --> 08:54.930
That sounds good.

08:54.930 --> 08:56.040
I wanna get some omelette soba.

08:56.320 --> 08:58.420
Why don't we invite Takayuki too?

08:58.710 --> 09:02.890
I guess it seems like Motoharu-san isn't 
working because Mima-san is working.

09:02.890 --> 09:03.940
I do work.

09:04.960 --> 09:05.970
Looks like they're having fun.

09:06.400 --> 09:08.230
Will one of you contact Takayuki?

09:08.230 --> 09:10.340
Yes! I'll do it!

09:10.340 --> 09:11.100
Well?

09:11.100 --> 09:11.940
Huh?

09:11.940 --> 09:14.470
Think you'll be able to do something 
amazing this summer break?

09:14.990 --> 09:16.000
Not at all.

09:16.000 --> 09:16.730
Oh?

09:17.240 --> 09:20.900
But days like this where nothing 
special happens are fun too.

09:21.260 --> 09:22.170
That's good enough.

09:23.830 --> 09:26.880
You should ask for candles on your 
birthday cake next year too.

09:26.880 --> 09:27.650
What?

09:27.650 --> 09:29.990
Why are we back on this topic?!

11:00.010 --> 11:05.010
<b>Coming up next</b>

11:00.010 --> 11:05.010
<b>Summer Festival</b>

11:05.020 --> 11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

11:05.020 --> 11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
